# Sourced pages are evidence: each is stored byte for byte, as fetched, and its SHA-256 is in the SHA256SUMS file beside it.
# Without this, core.autocrlf rewrote their line endings in the index, so a checkout could not give back the hashed bytes (§607).
**/raw/** -text
# The same for files a generated catalog pins by SHA-256 over their bytes (PS-6 US-3, §786): the generator's CSVs and the READ transcription
# it reads - core.autocrlf would hand a checkout CRLF where the digest was taken over LF.
usa/president_by_*.csv -text
usa/maine_districts_read_2012_2016.tsv -text
usa/house_*.csv -text
usa/senate_*.csv -text
usa/us_veto_measures.csv -text
